    "title": "I-Team: Gunfire at Shaw High School investigated - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ed Gallek Peggy Gallek Jordan Unger ,\n3 hours ago\nEAST CLEVELAND, Ohio (WJW) - The FOX 8 I-Team has found gunshots flew outside Shaw High School in East Cleveland with an armed male and a security officer firing shots.\nIt happened Thursday afternoon about 3:15 p.m. and no one was hurt. But now, the Cuyahoga County Sheriff's Department is investigating.\nOberlin professor, wife murdered: New details revealed after suspect appears in court Thursday evening, an I-Team camera saw investigators still on the scene.\n\"Preliminary information indicates that Security for the East Cleveland School System encountered a male with a firearm outside of Shaw High School. The male suspect discharged his firearm toward security, who then returned fire. No injuries were reported,\" a spokesperson for the county said.\nInvestigators said the suspect then ran from the scene.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Fox 8 Cleveland WJW.\n3",
